{%- comment -%}
  Besjaar 11.6.14 — desktop-only refinements that sit on top of the desktop
  carrier (kept separate so the large carrier is not rewritten for small
  changes; fold both into the desktop CSS during consolidation).

  - Hero, full-bleed (≥ 901px): the photo becomes the section background,
    edge to edge. On desktop the image is swapped for the lifestyle shot
    (besjaar-lifestyle-shower.webp) and the scene band gets the Besjaar lady shower lifestyle
    image (besjaar-lady-shower-desktop.webp) so the two never repeat;
    the swap is done by the script below with the asset URLs rendered
    here, and the hero image is faded in once swapped. Layering: the inner
    grid is left static so the image (z 0) is positioned against the
    section, the wash (section ::after, z 1) sits above it and the text
    column (z 3) above both. The text row keeps the page container width
    and the text column is inset a further clamp(32px, 7vw, 140px) from
    the container edge. Navy wash from the left, white text, white primary
    button; chips in the right corners. Height from clamp(560px, 78vh,
    800px).
  - Shop hub (/collections/all): the "Eén collectie…" banner is visually
    hidden on desktop (stays in the DOM as the page h1).
  - Product page: gallery capped to a 640px ice stage with the product
    blended onto it, thumbnails as square tiles centred beneath, summary
    type scaled up; the third-party "Secure Checkout With" badge block is
    hidden by the script (found by its heading text, never touching the
    theme's own buttons).
  - About page (sections/main-page, about branch): navy/ice palette, the
    brand stage becomes a wordmark card with a product packshot blended
    onto ice (first filter model without hose, else the first product),
    the four category cards get cover photos from theme assets, the
    principles/story/service blocks get tiles. Asset and image URLs are
    rendered as custom properties on <body> below.
  - Trust strip: continuous loop on wide screens (see script).
  - Header search pill forced into one row.
  - Feature cards, bento: first card tall on the left, two stacked rows on
    the right.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
<script type="application/json" id="bj-desktop-hero-swap">{"hero":{{ 'besjaar-hero-premium-spa.webp' | asset_url | json }},"scene":{{ 'besjaar-lady-shower-desktop.webp' | asset_url | json }}}</script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'page' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign bj_about_product = blank
    for bj_p in collections['all'].products
      if bj_about_product == blank and bj_p.featured_image != blank and bj_p.title contains 'Filter'
        unless bj_p.title contains 'Slang' or bj_p.title contains 'Navulset'
          assign bj_about_product = bj_p
        endunless
      endif
    endfor
    if bj_about_product == blank
      assign bj_about_product = collections['all'].products.first
    endif
    assign bj_about_stage = ''
    if bj_about_product != blank and bj_about_product.featured_image != blank
      assign bj_about_stage = bj_about_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900
    endif
  -%}
  <style>body[data-page-type="page"]{--bj-about-stage:url({{ bj_about_stage }});--bj-about-1:url({{ 'besjaar-web-real-modes.webp' | asset_url }});--bj-about-2:url({{ 'besjaar-macro-nozzles.webp' | asset_url }});--bj-about-3:url({{ 'besjaar-premium-hero-pressure-v3.webp' | asset_url }});--bj-about-4:url({{ 'besjaar-lifestyle-shower.webp' | asset_url }})}</style>
{%- endif -%}
